Prompt Optimizer & Compiler 🚀

A lightning-fast, zero-dependency vanilla JavaScript application designed to optimize raw user prompts and compile them into structured, professional agent instructions.

Features

Step 1: Input - Accept raw, unstructured thoughts or instructions.

Step 2: Optimize - Automatically refines prompts for clarity, constraints, and conciseness using the Gemini API.

Step 3: Compile - Structures the optimized prompt into a standard Agent format (Objective, Inputs, Constraints, Steps, Output).

Local First - Features debounced localStorage caching so you never lose your work if you accidentally refresh or close the tab.

Zero Dependencies - Built entirely with HTML, CSS, and Vanilla JS. No React, no Webpack, no bloat.

Prerequisites

To run this application locally, you will need:

A modern web browser.

A Google Gemini API Key.

Installation & Setup

Clone the repository:

git clone [https://github.com/yourusername/prompt-optimizer.git](https://github.com/yourusername/prompt-optimizer.git)
cd prompt-optimizer


Configure Environment:

Copy the .env.example file to .env.

Add your Gemini API key.

Note: Since this is a client-side application, you will need to inject this environment variable via your build tool or implement a lightweight backend proxy to secure your API key in production.

Run Locally:
Because this is a static site, you can simply open index.html in your browser, or serve it via a local development server:

npx serve .
# or
python3 -m http.server 8000
